│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ beam_local_schedule_search                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the sampled greedy construction with a deterministic beam search followed by      │
│                          │ transaction-order local search.                                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. The previous method evaluates only a small random subset of remaining transactions at  │
│                          │ every position. It can therefore discard the transaction whose placement avoids later     │
│                          │ read/write conflict chains.                                                               │
│                          │ 2. The new beam search expands several low-cost partial transaction orders                │
│                          │ simultaneously. Each expansion uses `workload.get_opt_seq_cost`, so ranking is based      │
│                          │ directly on the actual scheduling makespan rather than transaction length or write        │
│                          │ counts.                                                                                   │
│                          │ 3. Greedy completions from several distinct starting transactions provide additional      │
│                          │ diverse complete schedules. This avoids beam-search tie breaking concentrating entirely   │
│                          │ on one early ordering.                                                                    │
│                          │ 4. Each promising complete schedule is improved using best insertion moves. Moving one    │
│                          │ transaction from one position to another can eliminate long conflict-induced critical     │
│                          │ paths that cannot be repaired by a purely prefix-greedy method.                           │
│                          │ 5. A cost cache prevents repeated simulator calls for the same order. The search width is │
│                          │ bounded by `num_seqs`, keeping the method practical while using substantially more of the │
│                          │ available scheduling information than random sampling.                                    │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0329                                                                                   │
