│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ multistart_cost_search                                                                    │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the single sampled greedy construction with a multi-start, cost-driven search.    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. The previous implementation ignored `num_seqs`, sampled only up to ten possible next   │
│                          │ transactions, and returned one random construction. It could therefore miss the           │
│                          │ transaction whose placement produces the lowest actual prefix makespan.                   │
│                          │ 2. The new construction uses several starts (`num_seqs`) and evaluates a substantially    │
│                          │ broader candidate set at every position using `workload.get_opt_seq_cost`. This directly  │
│                          │ optimizes the simulator’s real conflict-aware objective instead of relying on transaction │
│                          │ length or write-count proxies.                                                            │
│                          │ 3. Prefix costs are cached, avoiding repeated schedule evaluations across starts and      │
│                          │ local optimization.                                                                       │
│                          │ 4. After choosing the best greedy schedule, a conflict-aware local search tests adjacent  │
│                          │ swaps, arbitrary swaps, and insertion moves. These changes can move a transaction before  │
│                          │ or after the transactions with which it causes expensive read/write conflict delay.       │
│                          │ 5. For very small workloads, exhaustive permutation enumeration is used, guaranteeing an  │
│                          │ optimal makespan rather than merely a heuristic result.                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The result retains valid transaction permutations while spending the search budget on     │
│                          │ schedules measured by the exact makespan evaluator.                                       │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0383                                                                                   │
