│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ multistart_cost_search                                                                    │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the single sampled greedy construction with a multi-start, cost-driven search     │
│                          │ that uses the simulator’s actual makespan objective at every decision.                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. `num_seqs` is now used as the number of independent construction attempts instead of   │
│                          │ being ignored.                                                                            │
│                          │ 2. Each construction evaluates all remaining transactions for smaller workloads, or a     │
│                          │ broad random candidate set for larger workloads. It chooses the append operation with the │
│                          │ lowest actual prefix makespan, rather than considering only ten randomly drawn            │
│                          │ transactions.                                                                             │
│                          │ 3. Diverse starting transactions and randomized tie-breaking prevent all attempts from    │
│                          │ converging to the same greedy ordering.                                                   │
│                          │ 4. The best constructed ordering is refined using exact-cost adjacent swaps and insertion │
│                          │ moves. These moves directly repair poor early greedy choices and are accepted only when   │
│                          │ they lower the complete workload makespan.                                                │
│                          │ 5. A per-call cost cache avoids repeated simulator evaluations for schedules reached by   │
│                          │ multiple local-search moves.                                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This focuses optimization on read/write-conflict delay as measured by `get_opt_seq_cost`, │
│                          │ rather than transaction length or write-count proxies.                                    │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
