├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ elite_exchange_refinement                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ Refine several strong greedy seeds instead of only the single best initial order, and add │
│                          │ non-adjacent transaction exchanges to the local-search neighborhood.                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. The makespan landscape for conflict-constrained transaction orders is non-convex: a    │
│                          │ schedule that is slightly worse before local search can reach a better basin after        │
│                          │ transactions are moved.                                                                   │
│                          │ 2. The current code discards all but one greedy result before refinement. Retaining the   │
│                          │ best three independent greedy constructions provides diversification with bounded         │
│                          │ additional work.                                                                          │
│                          │ 3. Insertion moves and adjacent swaps cannot always improve an ordering when two distant  │
│                          │ transactions must exchange positions together. An exhaustive pairwise exchange pass for   │
│                          │ small workloads directly tests these coordinated changes.                                 │
│                          │ 4. Exact objective evaluation remains cached, so candidates encountered in more than one  │
│                          │ neighborhood or elite refinement are not recomputed.                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This improves the chance of removing long conflict chains that greedy prefix construction │
│                          │ leaves behind, while preserving the existing exact makespan objective as the sole         │
│                          │ optimization criterion.                                                                   │
