│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ beam_local_schedule                                                                       │
│ patch_description        │ This version replaces random sampled greedy construction with a deterministic beam-search │
│                          │ and local-improvement optimizer.                                                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. For small workloads, it exhaustively evaluates all transaction permutations,           │
│                          │ guaranteeing the optimal schedule.                                                        │
│                          │ 2. For larger workloads, it keeps several high-quality partial schedules in a beam rather │
│                          │ than committing to one greedy choice.                                                     │
│                          │ 3. Each possible extension is evaluated using `workload.get_opt_seq_cost`, so decisions   │
│                          │ are based directly on the actual conflict-aware makespan rather than transaction length   │
│                          │ or write counts.                                                                          │
│                          │ 4. The best complete beam schedules are refined with insertion and swap local search.     │
│                          │ These moves can repair poor early ordering decisions and reduce conflict delays further.  │
│                          │ 5. Results are cached, avoiding repeated simulator evaluations for identical prefixes or  │
│                          │ complete schedules.                                                                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This should consistently outperform the previous single random greedy path while          │
│                          │ preserving the same input/output interface.                                               │
