│ patch_name               │ pair_swap_descent                                                                         │
│ patch_description        │ Add a conflict-aware non-adjacent exchange neighborhood after insertion refinement.       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. Adjacent exchanges only repair local inversions, while insertion moves can still miss  │
│                          │ schedules where two distant transactions must exchange places simultaneously.             │
│                          │ 2. A non-adjacent swap directly tests this important ordering change using the exact      │
│                          │ `get_opt_seq_cost` objective, rather than transaction-size proxies.                       │
│                          │ 3. For small workloads, all pairs are evaluated; for large workloads, a broad randomized  │
│                          │ pair sample controls runtime.                                                             │
│                          │ 4. Repeating best-improving pair swaps allows the search to remove several long-range     │
│                          │ conflict-ordering mistakes. The existing cost cache avoids re-evaluating schedules        │
│                          │ already examined by other neighborhoods.                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This expands the local-search neighborhood without changing schedule validity or relying  │
│                          │ on approximate conflict estimates.                                                        │
