│ patch_name               │ beam_vnd_scheduler                                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ This version combines the sampled greedy construction from the earlier program with the   │
│                          │ stronger cached local-search approach from the current program.                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key improvements:                                                                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. Exact small-instance optimization: workloads with at most eight transactions are       │
│                          │ evaluated exhaustively, guaranteeing the minimum makespan.                                │
│                          │ 2. Beam-guided greedy construction: instead of committing to only one greedy prefix,      │
│                          │ several promising partial transaction orders are retained. This avoids losing good        │
│                          │ schedules because of an early locally-optimal decision.                                   │
│                          │ 3. Multiple randomized greedy seeds: sampled candidate selection preserves                │
│                          │ diversification for large workloads and supplements the beam search with independent      │
│                          │ schedules.                                                                                │
│                          │ 4. Cached exact schedule costs: every prefix and complete-order evaluation is memoized,   │
│                          │ so repeated local-search comparisons are inexpensive.                                     │
│                          │ 5. Variable-neighborhood descent: insertion moves, distant swaps, and segment reversals   │
│                          │ are explored. These neighborhoods can repair different classes of conflict-ordering       │
│                          │ mistakes that adjacent swaps alone cannot resolve.                                        │
│                          │ 6. Elite refinement: both beam-generated and greedy-generated schedules are considered,   │
│                          │ since a non-best initial schedule can become best after local optimization.               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Together, beam construction improves global choices while the conflict-aware local search │
│                          │ removes residual ordering inversions, leading to lower makespan schedules.                │
