│ patch_type               │ cross                                                                                     │
│ patch_name               │ beam_vnd_scheduler                                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ This version combines the prior objective-driven greedy construction with a stronger      │
│                          │ beam-search and variable-neighborhood local improvement strategy.                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. Every decision is evaluated using `workload.get_opt_seq_cost`, so ordering decisions   │
│                          │ directly optimize the true conflict-delay makespan rather than proxy metrics such as      │
│                          │ transaction length.                                                                       │
│                          │ 2. A bounded beam search retains several promising partial schedules instead of           │
│                          │ committing to one greedy prefix. This prevents early local choices from permanently       │
│                          │ blocking better conflict orderings.                                                       │
│                          │ 3. Independent greedy constructions provide diversity, including different starting       │
│                          │ transactions and randomized candidate pools for larger workloads.                         │
│                          │ 4. The best complete schedules are refined using insertion and swap neighborhoods.        │
│                          │ Insertions are particularly useful for moving a transaction around a conflict chain,      │
│                          │ while swaps can repair non-local ordering mistakes.                                       │
│                          │ 5. Costs are cached by sequence, avoiding repeated simulator evaluations for prefixes and │
│                          │ neighboring schedules encountered multiple times.                                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The search remains bounded for large workloads through candidate and neighborhood         │
│                          │ sampling, while using exhaustive candidate evaluation and local neighborhoods for smaller │
│                          │ workloads where doing so is affordable.                                                   │
