                        Patch Metadata - Gen 11/200 - Novelty: 1/3 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/3                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ destroy_repair_refinement                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ Add a bounded destroy-and-repair phase after the existing greedy and local-search         │
│                          │ refinement.                                                                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The current relocation/swap search can only make improvements reachable through a single  │
│                          │ local move. Transactional conflict makespan landscapes often contain local minima where   │
│                          │ several transactions must be reordered together before the critical read/write dependency │
│                          │ chain improves. The new phase escapes these minima by:                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. Removing a small neighborhood of 3–6 transactions from the refined schedule.           │
│                          │ 2. Using both contiguous removals, which can reorder a conflict-heavy schedule region,    │
│                          │ and random removals, which can reconnect distant conflicting transactions.                │
│                          │ 3. Rebuilding the removed portion greedily by evaluating every removed transaction at     │
│                          │ every insertion point with the simulator’s actual sequence cost.                          │
│                          │ 4. Accepting only complete repaired schedules that reduce the measured makespan.          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This is a large-neighborhood search directly guided by exact simulator costs rather than  │
│                          │ operation-count proxies. It preserves the strong ordering already found for unaffected    │
│                          │ transactions while allowing coordinated multi-transaction reorderings that insertion/swap │
│                          │ VND cannot reach.                                                                         │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0269                                                                                   │
