│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ adaptive_lns_repair                                                                       │
│ patch_description        │ This implementation replaces the prefix beam search with an adaptive large-neighborhood   │
│                          │ search (ALNS) approach:                                                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. It builds several diverse objective-guided schedules using randomized greedy           │
│                          │ construction.                                                                             │
│                          │ 2. It scores every tested partial or complete ordering using `workload.get_opt_seq_cost`, │
│                          │ rather than relying on transaction size or write counts.                                  │
│                          │ 3. It repeatedly destroys portions of elite schedules by removing transactions from       │
│                          │ random, contiguous, and high-disruption regions.                                          │
│                          │ 4. It repairs each destroyed schedule by greedily selecting the transaction-position      │
│                          │ insertion with the lowest exact simulator cost.                                           │
│                          │ 5. It applies targeted relocation and swap improvements to completed schedules.           │
│                          │ 6. It preserves an elite pool of different good schedules, allowing the search to escape  │
│                          │ local minima instead of optimizing only one greedy schedule.                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Destroy-and-repair changes multiple transaction relationships simultaneously, which can   │
│                          │ discover schedules unavailable to simple swaps, insertions, or beam-prefix decisions.     │
