│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ destroy_repair_refinement                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ Add a simulator-guided destroy-and-repair phase after the existing local search.          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. The current refinement stops at a local optimum under swaps and insertions.            │
│                          │ Transaction-ordering objectives commonly contain larger basins where several transactions │
│                          │ must move together before an improvement becomes visible.                                 │
│                          │ 2. Each destroy attempt removes a small group of transactions from the incumbent          │
│                          │ schedule. The group is selected partly from a contiguous region, which targets correlated │
│                          │ conflict decisions, and partly from dispersed positions, which targets independent        │
│                          │ long-range interactions.                                                                  │
│                          │ 3. The removed transactions are greedily reinserted into every possible position using    │
│                          │ the exact simulator objective already cached by `schedule_cost`. This ensures repair      │
│                          │ decisions optimize actual makespan rather than proxy features such as transaction length  │
│                          │ or write count.                                                                           │
│                          │ 4. Any improved repaired schedule is locally refined again. Thus, destroy-and-repair      │
│                          │ creates an escape move while the existing swap/insertion VND exploits the new promising   │
│                          │ region thoroughly.                                                                        │
│                          │ 5. The phase is bounded by both transaction count and `num_seqs`, preserving predictable  │
│                          │ runtime while providing several structurally different escapes from the initial local     │
│                          │ minimum.                                                                                  │
