│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ ruin_recreate_memetic                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ This version replaces the primarily prefix-beam-driven strategy with a memetic search     │
│                          │ combining three complementary mechanisms:                                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Diversified actual-cost construction:** transaction orders are built from several    │
│                          │ deterministic and randomized starts. Every extension is evaluated through the workload    │
│                          │ simulator, so decisions are based on measured prefix makespan rather than superficial     │
│                          │ transaction metadata.                                                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **Local ordering optimization:** strong seed schedules are improved with exact         │
│                          │ adjacent swaps, insertions, long swaps, and segment reversals. These moves directly       │
│                          │ change conflict orientation between transactions and are accepted only when they reduce   │
│                          │ the real simulated makespan.                                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 3. **Ruin-and-recreate search:** local minima often require changing several related      │
│                          │ conflict decisions together. The algorithm removes a conflict-sensitive subset of         │
│                          │ transactions from a good order, then reinserts them one at a time at their best measured  │
│                          │ positions. This can rebuild problematic regions without discarding the useful structure   │
│                          │ of the rest of the schedule.                                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ For small workloads, all permutations are still evaluated exactly. A schedule-cost cache  │
│                          │ avoids repeatedly simulating the same transaction sequence.                               │
