│ patch_name               │ destroy_repair_refinement                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the current prefix-shuffle perturbation with a simulator-guided                   │
│                          │ destroy-and-repair neighborhood. Prefix shuffling discards many useful pairwise conflict  │
│                          │ orientations at once and only rebuilds the suffix, whereas destroy-and-repair retains     │
│                          │ most of a strong local optimum and selectively repositions a small conflict-heavy region. │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The new helper removes either a contiguous block or scattered transactions, then          │
│                          │ reinserts each removed transaction at the position with the lowest exact simulated        │
│                          │ makespan. This directly evaluates the transaction conflict effects rather than relying on │
│                          │ transaction size or random ordering. Applying several repairs to the best refined         │
│                          │ schedules creates moves that cannot be reached by a single insertion, swap, or reversal   │
│                          │ descent, while the subsequent exact local refinement recovers any remaining small         │
│                          │ improvements.                                                                             │
