│ patch_description        │ This version combines exact-cost greedy construction, elite multi-start selection, local  │
│                          │ search, segment reversal, and destroy-and-repair large-neighborhood search.               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. It evaluates every greedy next-transaction choice using `workload.get_opt_seq_cost`,   │
│                          │ so choices are driven by actual conflict-induced makespan rather than operation counts.   │
│                          │ 2. It uses multiple shuffled starting transactions, retaining several elite schedules     │
│                          │ because greedy construction is path dependent.                                            │
│                          │ 3. It improves elite schedules using exact full-schedule relocation, distant swaps, and   │
│                          │ segment reversals.                                                                        │
│                          │ 4. It applies destroy-and-repair to move several transactions jointly across local        │
│                          │ minima. Each reinserted transaction and insertion position is evaluated using the exact   │
│                          │ simulator cost.                                                                           │
│                          │ 5. All evaluated schedules are cached, avoiding repeated simulator work during            │
│                          │ overlapping local-search neighborhoods.                                                   │
│                          │ 6. Every returned schedule remains a permutation of all transaction indices and preserves │
│                          │ the original input/output interface.                                                      │
