│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ two_step_greedy_lookahead                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ Replace purely myopic greedy selection with an exact two-transaction rollout score. The   │
│                          │ existing greedy constructor selects the next transaction only by the makespan of the      │
│                          │ current prefix. A transaction that is inexpensive immediately can nevertheless force a    │
│                          │ costly conflict chain with all subsequent transactions.                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ For every possible next transaction, this edit evaluates a bounded set of possible        │
│                          │ follow-up transactions using the simulator’s exact objective. It ranks the next           │
│                          │ transaction by the best achievable depth-two prefix makespan, while retaining the         │
│                          │ one-step score as a tie-breaker. This directly accounts for whether selecting a           │
│                          │ transaction now creates avoidable read/write conflict delay at the next scheduling        │
│                          │ decision.                                                                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The follow-up set is exhaustive for small remaining sets and sampled for large workloads, │
│                          │ preserving practical runtime while substantially reducing early greedy mistakes. Beam     │
│                          │ search and local search remain intact, so this adds higher-quality diversified seed       │
│                          │ schedules for later refinement.                                                           │
