│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ exact_beam_lns                                                                            │
│ patch_description        │ This version replaces single-path greedy construction with an exact-cost beam search      │
│                          │ followed by large-neighborhood optimization.                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Beam construction:** Rather than committing to one transaction at every prefix, it   │
│                          │ keeps multiple promising partial schedules. Every extension is scored by the simulator’s  │
│                          │ real prefix makespan.                                                                     │
│                          │ 2. **Diverse beam retention:** The beam retains low-cost prefixes while preferring        │
│                          │ different last transactions, preventing all candidates from collapsing into the same      │
│                          │ greedy path.                                                                              │
│                          │ 3. **Elite refinement:** The best complete beam schedules are improved with exact-cost    │
│                          │ insertion, swap, reversal, and short block-relocation neighborhoods.                      │
│                          │ 4. **Destroy-and-repair:** When local search stalls, a subset of transactions is removed  │
│                          │ and greedily reinserted using exact simulator costs. This can cross local minima          │
│                          │ requiring several related read/write-conflicting transactions to move together.           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The approach is fundamentally different from repeated greedy starts: it searches multiple │
│                          │ ordering prefixes simultaneously and only uses the simulator objective to make decisions. │
