╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ adaptive_diverse_beam                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ Replace independent append-only greedy restarts with a conflict-cost beam search over     │
│                          │ transaction prefixes.                                                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. Each beam state is a partial transaction order scored by the simulator’s exact prefix  │
│                          │ makespan objective.                                                                       │
│                          │ 2. At every depth, the search expands every retained prefix with every remaining          │
│                          │ transaction, allowing it to compare competing conflict orientations rather than           │
│                          │ committing permanently to one greedy choice.                                              │
│                          │ 3. The beam preserves diversity by first retaining the best prefix for distinct first     │
│                          │ transactions and, in the early levels, distinct first two-transaction orientations. This  │
│                          │ avoids losing schedules whose initial prefix looks equivalent but produces better         │
│                          │ downstream conflict overlap.                                                              │
│                          │ 4. The beam grows adaptively when the score at the cutoff is tied, because tied prefix    │
│                          │ costs are precisely where greedy selection has insufficient information about future      │
│                          │ read/write conflicts.                                                                     │
│                          │ 5. The existing local search and destroy/repair phases remain unchanged and refine the    │
│                          │ best complete beam schedule, so this improves construction quality without rewriting the  │
│                          │ optimizer.                                                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This should find better global transaction orders when multiple prefix choices have       │
│                          │ similar immediate makespans but different future serialization consequences.              │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0230                                                                                   │
