│ patch_name               │ beam_ruin_hybrid                                                                          │
│ patch_description        │ This crossover restores the stronger beam/GRASP/local-search structure from the best      │
│                          │ prior implementation while retaining the current program’s exact-cost caching and         │
│                          │ large-neighborhood reconstruction strategy.                                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Step-by-step:                                                                             │
│                          │ 1. Small workloads are solved exactly by enumerating all transaction orders.              │
│                          │ 2. A conflict-aware beam search evaluates actual prefix makespans, preserving several     │
│                          │ promising dependency orientations rather than committing to a single greedy prefix.       │
│                          │ 3. Independent deterministic and randomized restricted-candidate greedy schedules add     │
│                          │ diverse seeds that can avoid beam-search local bias.                                      │
│                          │ 4. Elite schedules are improved with exact simulated makespan comparisons over insertion, │
│                          │ swap, and reversal neighborhoods.                                                         │
│                          │ 5. The best local optima receive destroy-and-repair moves, allowing coordinated           │
│                          │ reinsertion of conflict-heavy transactions and escape from local minima.                  │
│                          │ 6. Every scheduling decision is evaluated with `workload.get_opt_seq_cost`, so            │
│                          │ optimization directly targets the true makespan rather than surrogate transaction         │
│                          │ statistics.                                                                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This combines broad construction diversity with deeper exact-cost refinement, which is    │
│                          │ particularly effective for read/write conflict workloads where beneficial transaction     │
│                          │ ordering may require several coordinated moves.                                           │
